Vulnerability advisory data
===========================

`vulnerabilities.jsonl` in this ruleset is derived from the OSV.dev aggregated
database (https://osv.dev). Upstream sources include:

- GitHub Advisory Database (CC-BY 4.0)
  https://github.com/github/advisory-database
- PyPI Advisory Database (CC-BY 4.0)
  https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database
- Python Software Foundation advisory database (CC-BY 4.0)
  https://github.com/psf/advisory-database
- OpenSSF Malicious Packages (Apache-2.0)
  https://github.com/ossf/malicious-packages
- NVD CVEs converted to OSV by the OSV.dev project

Advisory identifiers, affected version ranges, severity buckets and one-line
summaries are reproduced and transformed. Duplicate records pointing at the
same advisory are merged, summaries are truncated to 180 characters, and only
a subset of packages is included. This file is therefore a transformed subset,
not a verbatim copy, of any upstream database.

Regenerate with `tools/refresh_vulnerability_db.py`. If an upstream source
changes its license, update this notice and `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` in the
same change.
